; Tutorial_3_Open_a_Database_and_Move_Through_Records.inix -- finding your way in RadioTrail, and playing a station.

[about]
Title=3 - Open a Database and Move Through Records
Intro=RadioTrail, the database DbDo opens first, explored by row, by column, by search and by record number, and a station played in the Homer Player.
Setup=DbDo is installed; on a first run it opens RadioTrail.
Homework=Find a station by keyword, then play it with Alt plus Shift plus P.

[step]

Say=One want: a station found and playing, quickly. The first time DbDo starts, it opens RadioTrail, a list of internet radio stations to search, sort and play.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Alt plus Control plus D, D for DbDo, opens it or brings it forward.
Key=Alt+Control+D
Hear=DbDo
Hear=DbDo ready

[step]

Say=Shift plus Z says where I am: the stations table of RadioTrail. Another database opens with Control plus O, O for Open, and the templates are in the Help menu, under Template Databases.
Key=Shift+Z
Hear=(stations, the number of stations, no filter, sorted by name)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Down Arrow moves by record; Right Arrow by column. Control plus G, G for Go, goes to a record by its number.
Key=Control+G
Hear=Go to Record dialog
Hear=Record number: edit
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I type 7 and press Enter.
Key=Enter
Hear=(record 7, its first column first)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus K, K for Keywords, searches every column for words.
Key=Control+K
Hear=Keywords dialog
Hear=Keywords: edit
Hear=Type in text.
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I type jazz and press Enter.
Key=Enter
Hear=(the first station holding jazz)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=F3 goes to the next match, Shift plus F3 to the one before. Alt plus Delete says the column and the row number.
Key=Alt+Delete
Hear=(the column's name and the row number)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=A planned misstep: Control plus F is not find here. In DbDo, F is for Filter, a later walk. Keywords is K. Escape leaves anything opened by mistake.
Key=Escape
Hear=DbDo
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Keywords searches every column; Jump searches one. Control plus J, Jump to Record, asks which column and what to look for.
Key=Control+J
Hear=Jump to Record dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I choose country, type Canada, and press Enter. The cursor lands on the first station there.
Key=Enter
Hear=(Canada, country, its row)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus Shift plus J jumps backward to the one before, and Control plus Shift plus K does the same for Keywords: Shift reverses, here as everywhere in DbDo.
Key=Control+Shift+J
Hear=(Canada, country, an earlier row)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Shift plus Y, Say Yield, says how many records there are.
Key=Shift+Y
Hear=(the number of stations)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Shift plus C, Say Cell, says the value under the cursor again, without moving.
Key=Shift+C
Hear=Canada
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus I, Inspect Record, shows the whole record at once, one field to a line: the station's name, genre, language and stream address among them. Escape closes it.
Key=Control+I
Hear=Inspect Record dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Now the reason RadioTrail opens first. Alt plus Shift plus P, Play Stream, plays the current station in the Homer Player, the same player FileDir uses.
Key=Alt+Shift+P
Hear=(the Homer Player, playing the station)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape closes the player and returns to the station I was on, ready for the next one.
Key=Escape
Hear=(stations, the same row)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=A database can hold several tables; Control plus T, Choose Table, lists them. Escape keeps the table I am in.
Key=Control+T
Hear=(Choose Table dialog, stations first)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape. RadioTrail is one table, easy to hold in mind. The next walk opens JobTrail, whose tables are linked to one another.
Key=Escape
Hear=stations
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.
